cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Mentor::i or the evaluation methodology in your own work, please cite both the paper and this software."
type: software
title: "Mentor::i: an open-source multi-agent workspace for the life-science literature"
abstract: >-
  Mentor::i is an open-source multi-agent scientific workspace for the
  life-science literature that orchestrates local and cloud-hosted large
  language models. This repository accompanies the paper "Systematic ablation
  of a multi-agent language model system for life sciences research" (Bianchi
  & Schokker, Communications AI & Computing), which ablates Mentor::i across
  11 pipeline settings in 22 experiments (244 expert-curated questions on 50
  papers among 200; over 1.18 million model calls) and reads every answer with
  three signals that check each other: a language model judge, concept recall
  against expert answers and claim checking against the source papers. The
  folder analysis/ holds the scripts that reproduce the paper's figures, tables
  and numbers; the data are in the Zenodo record doi:10.5281/zenodo.24143367.
